b>Pidurutalagala</b>, or previously <b>Mount Pedro</b> in English, is the highest mountain in Sri Lanka, at 2,524\u00a0m (8,281\u00a0ft). It is situated North-North-East from the town of Nuwara Eliya and is easily visible from most areas of the Central Province.</p>"}